<case xmlns="http://www.omg.org/spec/CMMN/20151109/MODEL" xmlns:cafienne="org.cafienne" id="employeecase.case" name="employeecase" expressionLanguage="spel" guid="_F01emp0">
    <documentation textFormat="text/plain">
        <text><![CDATA[Case of employee: one case per employee. FRD-02 scope (F01 onboarding + F02 probation): stage "Onboarding" (Onboarding checklist / Equipment request / Remaining setup / Onboarding overdue, milestone "Employee onboarded"), stage "Active employment" (entered on "Employee onboarded"; "Create development plan" for FRD-04), and the probation review (Probation review / Approve end of employment, milestone "Probation passed") per docs/features/FRD-02-onboarding-probation/spec.md section 8. Later features add their own stages to this same casePlanModel in their own gate 3.]]></text>
    </documentation>
    <caseFileModel typeRef="employeecase.type"/>
    <casePlanModel id="cm_employeecase.case_employeecase_0" name="Employee case" autoComplete="false">
        <documentation textFormat="text/plain">
            <text><![CDATA[autoComplete is deliberately false: this case represents the employee's whole lifecycle (hire to exit, like the legacy emp.case), so it must stay open after F01's onboarding tasks finish rather than closing the moment the one required-by-nothing-else task completes. Verified live (2026-10-15): with autoComplete=true and no requiredRule on "Equipment request", the case plan auto-completed as soon as "Onboarding checklist" finished, permanently stranding "Equipment request"/"Remaining setup" in state Available even after Onboarding.itRequestSent later became true. With autoComplete=false the case plan stays Active indefinitely, which is correct until a later feature (F08 offboarding) adds the real exitCriterion that should end the case.]]></text>
        </documentation>
        <processTask id="pi_release_onboarding_emails" name="Release onboarding emails" isBlocking="true" processRef="ReleaseOnboardingEmails.process">
            <documentation textFormat="text/plain">
                <text><![CDATA[Added 2026-10-21 ("mail triggered by the case engine"). No entryCriterion: active from
case start, same as "Onboarding checklist" below — the first thing this case does. Calls back
into hr-backend (ReleaseOnboardingEmails.process) the moment the case genuinely exists, which is
what releases "Welcome new employee" (held in hr-backend's own email_outbox) and triggers the
Keycloak set-password e-mail. Both are deliberately withheld at employee-creation time rather
than sent from there directly — see hr-backend's OnboardingService / OnboardingEmailReleaseService
/ EngineCallbackController for the full reasoning (they can't fire before the case exists, and
R-ARC-6's delivery guarantee still applies via OnboardingEmailReleaseScheduler's fallback if this
callback is ever lost).]]></text>
            </documentation>
            <inputs id="in_release_onboarding_emails_Employee" name="Employee" bindingRef="Employee"/>
            <parameterMapping id="pm_release_onboarding_emails_in_employeeId" sourceRef="in_release_onboarding_emails_Employee" targetRef="employeeId__roe001">
                <transformation id="pm_release_onboarding_emails_in_employeeId_t">
                    <body><![CDATA[Employee?.employeeId]]></body>
                </transformation>
            </parameterMapping>
        </processTask>
        <stage id="pi_stage_onboarding" name="Onboarding" autoComplete="true">
            <documentation textFormat="text/plain">
                <text><![CDATA[FRD-00 section 3 stage 1: starts when HR adds the employee (case start), ends when all mandatory checklist items are done (milestone "Employee onboarded"). autoComplete=true: completes once its active work is done; manual-activation items still Enabled (e.g. "Onboarding overdue" never needed) do not block it.]]></text>
            </documentation>
            <humanTask id="pi_onboarding_checklist" name="Onboarding checklist" isBlocking="true" performerRef="cr_employeecase_HR">
                <documentation textFormat="text/plain">
                    <text><![CDATA[Owner: HR. Active from case start. Completed once all mandatory checklist items are done (ONB-05); output sets Onboarding.completed, which raises the "Employee onboarded" milestone.]]></text>
                </documentation>
                <outputs id="out_onboarding_checklist_completed" name="Onboarding.completed" bindingRef="Onboarding"/>
                <extensionElements mustUnderstand="false">
                    <cafienne:implementation xmlns:cafienne="org.cafienne" humanTaskRef="onboardingchecklist.humantask">
                        <parameterMapping id="pm_onboarding_checklist_out_completed" sourceRef="completed__oc001" targetRef="out_onboarding_checklist_completed">
                            <transformation id="pm_onboarding_checklist_out_completed_t">
                                <body><![CDATA[{'completed':completed}]]></body>
                            </transformation>
                        </parameterMapping>
                        <duedate id="dd_onboarding_checklist" contextRef="Employee">
                            <condition id="dd_onboarding_checklist_cond">
                                <body><![CDATA[Employee.startDate == null ? null : (T(java.time.LocalDate).parse(Employee.startDate).atStartOfDay().toInstant(T(java.time.ZoneOffset).UTC)).toString()]]></body>
                            </condition>
                        </duedate>
                    </cafienne:implementation>
                </extensionElements>
            </humanTask>
            <milestone id="pi_employee_onboarded" name="Employee onboarded">
                <entryCriterion id="ec_employee_onboarded">
                    <planItemOnPart id="op_employee_onboarded" sourceRef="pi_onboarding_checklist">
                        <standardEvent>complete</standardEvent>
                    </planItemOnPart>
                </entryCriterion>
            </milestone>
            <humanTask id="pi_equipment_request" name="Equipment request" isBlocking="true" performerRef="cr_employeecase_ITAdmin">
                <documentation textFormat="text/plain">
                    <text><![CDATA[Owner: IT admin. Raised when HR sends the IT & equipment request (Onboarding.itRequestSent = true). Output sets Onboarding.itSetupComplete, computed by Spring from checklist_item.

    No entryCriterion here (removed 2026-10-16, Wave 1): a caseFileItemOnPart listening for an
    "update" transition on "Onboarding", gated by an ifPart on itRequestSent == true, looked right
    and was reported "verified live" on 2026-10-15, but that verification happened to be the FIRST
    update ever made to "Onboarding" in that test case. Confirmed live against the real engine
    (GET /cases/{id}/history/events, reproduced across a full engine process restart, not a
    transient hiccup): this onPart is evaluated only on the first-ever "Update" transition of a
    case-file item; every later update is logged by the engine as "Adding delayed event Update to
    myself" and never actually re-evaluated. In the real flow "Onboarding" is updated repeatedly
    before itRequestSent ever becomes true (checklist ticking updates mandatoryItemsDone first), so
    the onPart always exhausts itself on the wrong update and this task never activated. Plan-item
    onParts (e.g. "Remaining setup"'s, below) don't share this failure mode — a human task's own
    "complete" transition only happens once, same as "Employee onboarded"'s milestone sentry above,
    both of which fire reliably. OnboardingService.sendItRequest now drives this plan item directly
    via CaseEngineClient.startPlanItem (POST /cases/{id}/planitems/{id}/start) right after setting
    Onboarding.itRequestSent = true, instead of relying on a sentry confirmed broken for this shape
    of case-file item in this engine version (1.1.35).

    manualActivationRule = true (added 2026-10-19): with no entryCriterion and no manual activation,
    CMMN activates this task the moment the case plan starts, so IT would see it before HR ever sent
    the request and Spring's later "start" call would hit an already-Active item. With the rule it
    waits in Enabled until OnboardingService.sendItRequest starts it.

    Due date: Onboarding.itReadyBy, the HR-entered "ready by" date (F01 spec section 8), written into
    the case file by sendItRequest in the same update that sets itRequestSent.]]></text>
                </documentation>
                <itemControl id="ic_equipment_request">
                    <manualActivationRule id="mar_equipment_request">
                        <condition id="mar_equipment_request_cond">
                            <body><![CDATA[true]]></body>
                        </condition>
                    </manualActivationRule>
                </itemControl>
                <outputs id="out_equipment_request_itSetupComplete" name="Onboarding.itSetupComplete" bindingRef="Onboarding"/>
                <extensionElements mustUnderstand="false">
                    <cafienne:implementation xmlns:cafienne="org.cafienne" humanTaskRef="equipmentrequest.humantask">
                        <parameterMapping id="pm_equipment_request_out_itSetupComplete" sourceRef="itSetupComplete__eq001" targetRef="out_equipment_request_itSetupComplete">
                            <transformation id="pm_equipment_request_out_itSetupComplete_t">
                                <body><![CDATA[{'itSetupComplete':itSetupComplete}]]></body>
                            </transformation>
                        </parameterMapping>
                        <duedate id="dd_equipment_request" contextRef="Onboarding">
                            <condition id="dd_equipment_request_cond">
                                <body><![CDATA[Onboarding.itReadyBy == null ? null : (T(java.time.LocalDate).parse(Onboarding.itReadyBy).atStartOfDay().toInstant(T(java.time.ZoneOffset).UTC)).toString()]]></body>
                            </condition>
                        </duedate>
                    </cafienne:implementation>
                </extensionElements>
            </humanTask>
            <humanTask id="pi_remaining_setup" name="Remaining setup" isBlocking="true" performerRef="cr_employeecase_ITAdmin">
                <documentation textFormat="text/plain">
                    <text><![CDATA[Owner: IT admin. Raised only when "Equipment request" completes and IT work is still left (Onboarding.itSetupComplete != true), per F01 D-18. No case-file output.]]></text>
                </documentation>
                <entryCriterion id="ec_remaining_setup">
                    <ifPart contextRef="Onboarding">
                        <condition>
                            <body><![CDATA[Onboarding?.itSetupComplete != true]]></body>
                        </condition>
                    </ifPart>
                    <planItemOnPart id="op_remaining_setup" sourceRef="pi_equipment_request">
                        <standardEvent>complete</standardEvent>
                    </planItemOnPart>
                </entryCriterion>
                <extensionElements mustUnderstand="false">
                    <cafienne:implementation xmlns:cafienne="org.cafienne" humanTaskRef="remainingsetup.humantask">
                        <duedate id="dd_remaining_setup" contextRef="Onboarding">
                            <condition id="dd_remaining_setup_cond">
                                <body><![CDATA[Onboarding.itReadyBy == null ? null : (T(java.time.LocalDate).parse(Onboarding.itReadyBy).atStartOfDay().toInstant(T(java.time.ZoneOffset).UTC)).toString()]]></body>
                            </condition>
                        </duedate>
                    </cafienne:implementation>
                </extensionElements>
            </humanTask>
            <humanTask id="pi_onboarding_overdue" name="Onboarding overdue" isBlocking="true" performerRef="cr_employeecase_HR">
                <documentation textFormat="text/plain">
                    <text><![CDATA[Owner: HR. FRD-02 section 1: "If onboarding is still not complete 3 days after the start date (configurable, FRD-08), HR gets an 'Onboarding overdue' task." E1 fallback (03-case-file.md section 1): no native timer can read Onboarding.overdueDate, so manualActivationRule keeps this Enabled until hr-backend's OnboardingOverdueScheduler starts it (CaseEngineClient.startPlanItem) once the overdue date has passed. Exited as soon as "Onboarding checklist" completes, since the overdue condition is then gone. Due date: mirrored on Spring's engine_task row (F01 D-22 pattern).]]></text>
                </documentation>
                <exitCriterion id="xc_onboarding_overdue">
                    <planItemOnPart id="op_onboarding_overdue_exit" sourceRef="pi_onboarding_checklist">
                        <standardEvent>complete</standardEvent>
                    </planItemOnPart>
                </exitCriterion>
                <itemControl id="ic_onboarding_overdue">
                    <manualActivationRule id="mar_onboarding_overdue">
                        <condition id="mar_onboarding_overdue_cond">
                            <body><![CDATA[true]]></body>
                        </condition>
                    </manualActivationRule>
                </itemControl>
                <extensionElements mustUnderstand="false">
                    <cafienne:implementation xmlns:cafienne="org.cafienne" humanTaskRef="onboardingoverdue.humantask"/>
                </extensionElements>
            </humanTask>
        </stage>
        <stage id="pi_stage_active_employment" name="Active employment" autoComplete="false">
            <documentation textFormat="text/plain">
                <text><![CDATA[FRD-00 section 3 stage 2: starts when onboarding is complete (milestone "Employee onboarded"), ends when offboarding starts (FRD-07 adds that exit). Holds the three cycles of FRD-03/04/05; FRD-02 only adds "Create development plan".]]></text>
            </documentation>
            <entryCriterion id="ec_stage_active_employment">
                <planItemOnPart id="op_stage_active_employment" sourceRef="pi_employee_onboarded">
                    <standardEvent>occur</standardEvent>
                </planItemOnPart>
            </entryCriterion>
            <humanTask id="pi_create_development_plan" name="Create development plan" isBlocking="true" performerRef="cr_employeecase_Employee">
                <documentation textFormat="text/plain">
                    <text><![CDATA[Owner: Employee. FRD-02 section 2: when onboarding completes "The employee receives a 'Create development plan' task (FRD-04)". Active as soon as the stage starts. Completed by FRD-04's development plan screens (F05).]]></text>
                </documentation>
                <extensionElements mustUnderstand="false">
                    <cafienne:implementation xmlns:cafienne="org.cafienne" humanTaskRef="createdevelopmentplan.humantask"/>
                </extensionElements>
            </humanTask>
        </stage>
        <humanTask id="pi_probation_review" name="Probation review" isBlocking="true" performerRef="cr_employeecase_Manager">
            <documentation textFormat="text/plain">
                <text><![CDATA[Owner: Manager. FRD-02 section 2: "14 days before probation ends (configurable), the manager receives a 'Probation review' task." Case-plan level, not inside "Active employment", so a late onboarding can never block a review that is due. E1 fallback (03-case-file.md section 1): Spring writes Probation {reviewId, reviewDate} and its scheduler starts this item (manualActivationRule) once reviewDate has passed. Output: Probation.outcome (CONFIRM / END).]]></text>
            </documentation>
            <itemControl id="ic_probation_review">
                <manualActivationRule id="mar_probation_review">
                    <condition id="mar_probation_review_cond">
                        <body><![CDATA[true]]></body>
                    </condition>
                </manualActivationRule>
            </itemControl>
            <outputs id="out_probation_review_outcome" name="Probation.outcome" bindingRef="Probation"/>
            <extensionElements mustUnderstand="false">
                <cafienne:implementation xmlns:cafienne="org.cafienne" humanTaskRef="probationreview.humantask">
                    <parameterMapping id="pm_probation_review_out_outcome" sourceRef="outcome__pr001" targetRef="out_probation_review_outcome">
                        <transformation id="pm_probation_review_out_outcome_t">
                            <body><![CDATA[{'outcome':outcome}]]></body>
                        </transformation>
                    </parameterMapping>
                </cafienne:implementation>
            </extensionElements>
        </humanTask>
        <humanTask id="pi_approve_end_of_employment" name="Approve end of employment" isBlocking="true" performerRef="cr_employeecase_HR">
            <documentation textFormat="text/plain">
                <text><![CDATA[Owner: HR. ONB-08: "If probation ends with 'End employment', HR must approve before offboarding starts." Raised when "Probation review" completes with Probation.outcome == 'END'. Output: Probation.hrDecision (APPROVED / REJECTED).]]></text>
            </documentation>
            <entryCriterion id="ec_approve_end_of_employment">
                <ifPart contextRef="Probation">
                    <condition>
                        <body><![CDATA[Probation?.outcome == 'END']]></body>
                    </condition>
                </ifPart>
                <planItemOnPart id="op_approve_end_of_employment" sourceRef="pi_probation_review">
                    <standardEvent>complete</standardEvent>
                </planItemOnPart>
            </entryCriterion>
            <outputs id="out_approve_end_hrDecision" name="Probation.hrDecision" bindingRef="Probation"/>
            <extensionElements mustUnderstand="false">
                <cafienne:implementation xmlns:cafienne="org.cafienne" humanTaskRef="approveendofemployment.humantask">
                    <parameterMapping id="pm_approve_end_out_hrDecision" sourceRef="hrDecision__ae001" targetRef="out_approve_end_hrDecision">
                        <transformation id="pm_approve_end_out_hrDecision_t">
                            <body><![CDATA[{'hrDecision':hrDecision}]]></body>
                        </transformation>
                    </parameterMapping>
                </cafienne:implementation>
            </extensionElements>
        </humanTask>
        <milestone id="pi_probation_passed" name="Probation passed">
            <documentation textFormat="text/plain">
                <text><![CDATA["Confirm employment" records the milestone "Probation passed" (FRD-02 section 2). Also raised when HR rejects an "End employment" outcome: the employee is confirmed (FRD-02 spec D-P5, user decision 2026-10-21).]]></text>
            </documentation>
            <entryCriterion id="ec_probation_passed_confirm">
                <ifPart contextRef="Probation">
                    <condition>
                        <body><![CDATA[Probation?.outcome == 'CONFIRM']]></body>
                    </condition>
                </ifPart>
                <planItemOnPart id="op_probation_passed_confirm" sourceRef="pi_probation_review">
                    <standardEvent>complete</standardEvent>
                </planItemOnPart>
            </entryCriterion>
            <entryCriterion id="ec_probation_passed_rejected">
                <ifPart contextRef="Probation">
                    <condition>
                        <body><![CDATA[Probation?.hrDecision == 'REJECTED']]></body>
                    </condition>
                </ifPart>
                <planItemOnPart id="op_probation_passed_rejected" sourceRef="pi_approve_end_of_employment">
                    <standardEvent>complete</standardEvent>
                </planItemOnPart>
            </entryCriterion>
        </milestone>
    </casePlanModel>
    <caseRoles caseTeamRef="employeecase.caseteam"/>
    <input id="in_Employee" name="Employee" bindingRef="Employee"/>
    <input id="in_Onboarding" name="Onboarding" bindingRef="Onboarding"/>
    <input id="in_Probation" name="Probation" bindingRef="Probation"/>
</case>
